      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "The Coast Guard owns the sea. Continuing that vigilance – and our longstanding immigration enforcement mission – Coast Guard Cutter (CGC) Benjamin Bottoms (WPC-1132) interdicted 10 aliens aboard a 25-foot vessel in the vicinity of Point Loma. Through close coordination with Coast Guard Maritime Safety and Security Team Los Angeles/Long Beach and @CBP, CGC Benjamin Bottoms continued our efforts to detect, deter, and disrupt illeal maritime migration. \n\nThe Coast Guard continues to surge assets to counter Transnational Criminal Organizations, drug smugglers, and human traffickers wherever they move. Through the tireless efforts of Coast Guard men and women, we are controlling, securing, and defending our maritime borders. Through the ongoing vigilance of Coast Guard men and women, we are making America safer. \n\n#CoastGuard #MaritimeSafety #IllegalMigration #Teamwork #PointLoma",
      "text_resolved": "The Coast Guard owns the sea. Continuing that vigilance – and our longstanding immigration enforcement mission – Coast Guard Cutter (CGC) Benjamin Bottoms (WPC-1132) interdicted 10 aliens aboard a 25-foot vessel in the vicinity of Point Loma. Through close coordination with Coast Guard Maritime Safety and Security Team Los Angeles/Long Beach and @CBP, CGC Benjamin Bottoms continued our efforts to detect, deter, and disrupt illeal maritime migration. \n\nThe Coast Guard continues to surge assets to counter Transnational Criminal Organizations, drug smugglers, and human traffickers wherever they move. Through the tireless efforts of Coast Guard men and women, we are controlling, securing, and defending our maritime borders. Through the ongoing vigilance of Coast Guard men and women, we are making America safer. \n\n#CoastGuard #MaritimeSafety #IllegalMigration #Teamwork #PointLoma",
